            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "mozilla@keithcirkel.co.uk",
              "bug_id": 1977159,
              "count": 3,
              "creation_time": "2025-07-14T15:42:28Z",
              "creator": "mozilla@keithcirkel.co.uk",
              "id": 17580692,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "Looks like it's trying to postmessage to the main frame with the URL `https://*.anthropic.com` which Firefox considers an illegal host string. For a reduced example:\n\n```\ndata:text/html,<iframe id=i></iframe><script>i.contentWindow.parent.postMessage('foo', 'http://*.foo.com')</script>\n```\n\nNote that executing this page in Firefox will result in the SyntaxError:\n\n```\nDOMException: An invalid or illegal string was specified\n```\n\nWhile in Chrome we merely get a warning:\n\n```\nFailed to execute 'postMessage' on 'DOMWindow': The target origin provided ('http://%2A.foo.com') does not match the recipient window's origin ('null').\n```\n\nFurther, this seems to be in URL parsing. The JS expression `new URL('http://*.foo.com')` will result in an error in Firefox but not in Chrome.\n\nA quick gloss through the URL spec and I feel as though Chrome is correct here.",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "Looks like it's trying to postmessage to the main frame with the URL `https://*.anthropic.com` which Firefox considers an illegal host string. For a reduced example:\n\n```\ndata:text/html,<iframe id=i></iframe><script>i.contentWindow.parent.postMessage('foo', 'http://*.foo.com')</script>\n```\n\nNote that executing this page in Firefox will result in the SyntaxError:\n\n```\nDOMException: An invalid or illegal string was specified\n```\n\nWhile in Chrome we merely get a warning:\n\n```\nFailed to execute 'postMessage' on 'DOMWindow': The target origin provided ('http://%2A.foo.com') does not match the recipient window's origin ('null').\n```\n\nFurther, this seems to be in URL parsing. The JS expression `new URL('http://*.foo.com')` will result in an error in Firefox but not in Chrome.\n\nA quick gloss through the URL spec and I feel as though Chrome is correct here.",
              "time": "2025-07-14T15:42:28Z"
            },
